    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0635" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.4061 Motion Pictures/135</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4345</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-01">February 1,
                        1941</date>.<lb/>[Received February 28.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing the Embassy’s despatch No.
                    4244 dated January 16, 1941, transmitting a copy of a further note to the
                    Foreign Office requesting the immediate return of seven prints which belong to
                    Loew’s Incorporated and which were seized by the German authorities from
                    Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer A. G. of Berlin, I have the honor to report that the Foreign
                    Office has now finally acknowledged the Embassy’s notes of December 3,
                        1940,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d582-f1"/> and January 14, 1941,<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d582-f2"/> stating <pb facs="0636" n="624" xml:id="pg624"/> that “it
                    has requested the competent German internal authorities to give their
                    consideration to the matter and will inform the Embassy accordingly in due
                    course.”</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Chargé d’Affaires a. i. <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos</hi> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Warner</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Second Secretary of Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
